  "term": "childhood depression",
  "definition": "Childhood depression is a mental health condition in children marked by a lasting sad or irritable mood along with loss of interest in usual activities. It may also involve changes in sleep or appetite, low energy, feelings of worthlessness, or repeated thoughts about death or suicide.",
